(6663710, 996092, 108580, '<td valign="top">Very cool. Alien vs Predigator. Love the PP and the smooth dead space around the ''gator/croc, possibly masked and smoothed? The red pupil slit is most unusual and creepy. Top Marks (9)</td>', 'Very cool. Alien vs Predigator. Love the PP and the smooth dead space around the ''gator/croc, possibly masked and smoothed? The red pupil slit is most unusual and creepy. Top Marks (9)', '2012-02-04 10:33:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663712, 993085, 108580, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous. The light touching the foreground snow covered rocks is exasperatingly beautiful. Perfect timing in that. Dedication. If only you''d have cloned out the "dust/dirt" pixel speck in the middle of the water aaargh. Top Marks (9)</td>', 'Gorgeous. The light touching the foreground snow covered rocks is exasperatingly beautiful. Perfect timing in that. Dedication. If only you''d have cloned out the "dust/dirt" pixel speck in the middle of the water aaargh. Top Marks (9)', '2012-02-04 10:35:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663714, 994779, 108580, '<td valign="top">You''re back! Woo hoo. Ok this is so typical "Roz" quality. Either way magical macro of a robber-fly. I''m always sceptical of water drops on flowers, bugs etc but I am certain this is a "Roz" taken in the lawn morning grass dew and she has integrity. 9</td>', 'You''re back! Woo hoo. Ok this is so typical "Roz" quality. Either way magical macro of a robber-fly. I''m always sceptical of water drops on flowers, bugs etc but I am certain this is a "Roz" taken in the lawn morning grass dew and she has integrity. 9', '2012-02-04 10:36:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663715, 993867, 108580, '<td valign="top">That really is unique. A sense of mystery. There''s good flow in the image, partial S curve, and the way the light bathes through the grass highlighting every stem is beautiful. Film quality. I find that in the past few months entries are braver and less conformist to the crisp, shiny, over-saturated DPC formula shots. Encouraging...for photography. Top Marks (9)</td>', 'That really is unique. A sense of mystery. There''s good flow in the image, partial S curve, and the way the light bathes through the grass highlighting every stem is beautiful. Film quality. I find that in the past few months entries are braver and less conformist to the crisp, shiny, over-saturated DPC formula shots. Encouraging...for photography. Top Marks (9)', '2012-02-04 10:37:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663716, 996047, 108580, '<td valign="top">A pet (cat) photo that sweeps all others before it into the trash where imo many of them belong. That stare, the concentration is intense. Not only is it technically well photographed, PP''d and unique but it tells a typical feline vs Bird story and I hope it is being rewarded. Well done. Top Marks (9)</td>', 'A pet (cat) photo that sweeps all others before it into the trash where imo many of them belong. That stare, the concentration is intense. Not only is it technically well photographed, PP''d and unique but it tells a typical feline vs Bird story and I hope it is being rewarded. Well done. Top Marks (9)', '2012-02-04 10:37:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663717, 995715, 108580, '<td valign="top">In the Queens best English..."We are not amused"<br/>Fabulous bird shot, BG, crisp, composition and telling a story to which only bird ''togs can relate :) Top Marks (9)</td>', 'In the Queens best English..."We are not amused"Fabulous bird shot, BG, crisp, composition and telling a story to which only bird ''togs can relate :) Top Marks (9)', '2012-02-04 10:37:20.000000', NULL, 1),
