(6663828, 995523, 94265, '<td valign="top">A very well-taken modelling shot, nice focus and bokeh; I like the position of her face but I do wish her eyes were directed at the camera.</td>', 'A very well-taken modelling shot, nice focus and bokeh; I like the position of her face but I do wish her eyes were directed at the camera.', '2012-02-04 12:26:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663832, 994880, 94265, '<td valign="top">I''m almost sick to death of waterdrops on glass but this one is great; very interesting patterns in the background and they look cool in the droplets. I don''t mind the little pop of yellow, although I think I''d personally have prefered and all-over blue. Nice focus, well done.</td>', 'I''m almost sick to death of waterdrops on glass but this one is great; very interesting patterns in the background and they look cool in the droplets. I don''t mind the little pop of yellow, although I think I''d personally have prefered and all-over blue. Nice focus, well done.', '2012-02-04 12:29:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663835, 996453, 94265, '<td valign="top">Composition and contrast are lacking something for me but this is pretty creative, using an exisiting man-made structure to help create an almost abstract or surreal street-scape.</td>', 'Composition and contrast are lacking something for me but this is pretty creative, using an exisiting man-made structure to help create an almost abstract or surreal street-scape.', '2012-02-04 12:31:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663840, 995656, 94265, '<td valign="top">Nice to see an orchid(?) in b&amp;w, it lets the viewer concentrate fully on those wonderful shapes and patterns without any colour to distract.</td>', 'Nice to see an orchid(?) in b&w, it lets the viewer concentrate fully on those wonderful shapes and patterns without any colour to distract.', '2012-02-04 12:35:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663843, 994328, 94265, '<td valign="top">Lots to look at here, shapes, colours, textures; interesting and well-taken. I like the patch of visible sky too, nice moody clouds.</td>', 'Lots to look at here, shapes, colours, textures; interesting and well-taken. I like the patch of visible sky too, nice moody clouds.', '2012-02-04 12:37:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663848, 994487, 94265, '<td valign="top">What the Hell, it looks like he''s hurting her. :-O Unappealing content aside, this is a snapshot, not a high scorer for me.</td>', 'What the Hell, it looks like he''s hurting her. :-O Unappealing content aside, this is a snapshot, not a high scorer for me.', '2012-02-04 12:40:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663850, 995324, 94265, '<td valign="top">I''m not keen on the crop personally but the crisp focus is great. He has an interesting face. I feel with the negative space to his right, there was no need to crop off the side of his glasses or the bottom of his beard; I think this would have benefitted from his eyes looking off into that space. Still a very good shot overall though.</td>', 'I''m not keen on the crop personally but the crisp focus is great. He has an interesting face. I feel with the negative space to his right, there was no need to crop off the side of his glasses or the bottom of his beard; I think this would have benefitted from his eyes looking off into that space. Still a very good shot overall though.', '2012-02-04 12:42:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663851, 996126, 94265, '<td valign="top">Contrast could do with a boost but this is a lovely and very calming image.</td>', 'Contrast could do with a boost but this is a lovely and very calming image.', '2012-02-04 12:42:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663853, 993505, 94265, '<td valign="top">What a stunning cat. I like the title, it fits very well as the pristine white coat stands out a mile from the mucky surroundings and the cat does indeed look displeased! Nice crips focus. Well done!</td>', 'What a stunning cat. I like the title, it fits very well as the pristine white coat stands out a mile from the mucky surroundings and the cat does indeed look displeased! Nice crips focus. Well done!', '2012-02-04 12:44:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663860, 996054, 94265, '<td valign="top">This really made me smile. Nice clear focus, the sandy colours and blue sky compliment each other well, I like the perspective too. A 7 from me, those guys are awesome, lol.</td>', 'This really made me smile. Nice clear focus, the sandy colours and blue sky compliment each other well, I like the perspective too. A 7 from me, those guys are awesome, lol.', '2012-02-04 12:55:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663891, 996388, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great sense of texture here and articulation with the world. The marks are almost like a forensics story. I''m also intrigued by how flat it looks - the title implies a 3d structure but I struggle to discern it.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Minimal in the extreme - I don''t think it has enough visual critical mass to get going.<br/> <br/>Overall: Bold FS entry.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great sense of texture here and articulation with the world. The marks are almost like a forensics story. I''m also intrigued by how flat it looks - the title implies a 3d structure but I struggle to discern it. Critical stuff: Minimal in the extreme - I don''t think it has enough visual critical mass to get going. Overall: Bold FS entry.', '2012-02-04 13:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663893, 995707, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Composition over clarity - I like that. The washed out nature of the contrast, the utterly understated strength of the structure and the (nearly) negative space make for a most effective image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Too well balance to suggest any changes - I imagine that if you changed the slightest thing, the whole image would fall apart.<br/> <br/>Overall: A stunning example of how an image can be more than the sum of its parts.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Composition over clarity - I like that. The washed out nature of the contrast, the utterly understated strength of the structure and the (nearly) negative space make for a most effective image. Critical stuff: Too well balance to suggest any changes - I imagine that if you changed the slightest thing, the whole image would fall apart. Overall: A stunning example of how an image can be more than the sum of its parts.', '2012-02-04 13:56:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663894, 996274, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The horns of the shadows are magnificent, they get lost on their owners so the shadows rescue them from obscurity. I really like the flare at the top of the frame too.  The overall feeling is quite joyous and a little bit chilly!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing really.<br/> <br/>Overall: A lovely shot all round.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The horns of the shadows are magnificent, they get lost on their owners so the shadows rescue them from obscurity. I really like the flare at the top of the frame too.  The overall feeling is quite joyous and a little bit chilly! Critical stuff: Nothing really. Overall: A lovely shot all round.', '2012-02-04 13:59:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663895, 993492, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Reminiscent of a pigs head poking out of the coat (though my wife doesn''t no matter how many times I try to point it out). I also get the image of him standing on the terraces of a football (soccer) ground. I like the greenish colours and the grain too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing of note.<br/> <br/>Overall; An image you can have a conversation with. I like that.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Reminiscent of a pigs head poking out of the coat (though my wife doesn''t no matter how many times I try to point it out). I also get the image of him standing on the terraces of a football (soccer) ground. I like the greenish colours and the grain too. Critical stuff: Nothing of note. Overall; An image you can have a conversation with. I like that.', '2012-02-04 14:03:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663896, 995070, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great perspective and contrast - the rushing figure makes me wonder what he is leaving behind. I like how you have created a clear impression that his head has been cropped.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not a fan of the halo around the figure.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great vision, well executed.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great perspective and contrast - the rushing figure makes me wonder what he is leaving behind. I like how you have created a clear impression that his head has been cropped. Critical stuff: I''m not a fan of the halo around the figure. Overall: Great vision, well executed.', '2012-02-04 14:05:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663897, 993696, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Ben, I know this is yours but I''m not letting that exclude me from commenting or scoring. I love how relaxed this is - it makes me what to take a deep breath; it feels like a warm evening. The blurry ducks are amazing - just enough form to remain coherent. I''m particularly fond of the trees in the background and how they seem to be illuminated. Of course, your daughter is so important. Like a catalyst, I feel she doesn''t take an active role in the image but none of it would work if she were absent.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not sure I like that lighter area below the wall of the left edge of the frame.<br/> <br/>Overall: Marvellously understated stuff.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Ben, I know this is yours but I''m not letting that exclude me from commenting or scoring. I love how relaxed this is - it makes me what to take a deep breath; it feels like a warm evening. The blurry ducks are amazing - just enough form to remain coherent. I''m particularly fond of the trees in the background and how they seem to be illuminated. Of course, your daughter is so important. Like a catalyst, I feel she doesn''t take an active role in the image but none of it would work if she were absent. Critical stuff: I''m not sure I like that lighter area below the wall of the left edge of the frame. Overall: Marvellously understated stuff.', '2012-02-04 14:11:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663899, 996426, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This feels like I''ve turned a page in an art house photography magazine - perhaps ''Color''. The image is bold, highly communicative but still obscure. We are left with many questions. The toning is perfect and the crispness of the rendition adds much, as does th reflected sky.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I suppose in the end, the mystery of the image frustrates as much as it it delights.<br/> <br/>Overall: A highly intriguing and well-made image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This feels like I''ve turned a page in an art house photography magazine - perhaps ''Color''. The image is bold, highly communicative but still obscure. We are left with many questions. The toning is perfect and the crispness of the rendition adds much, as does th reflected sky. Critical stuff: I suppose in the end, the mystery of the image frustrates as much as it it delights. Overall: A highly intriguing and well-made image.', '2012-02-04 14:20:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6663900, 996047, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: DPC is full of cat shots - but this one transcends indulgent pet sentimentality and delivers an unexpected killer punch. The bird on the TV(?) and the transfixed kit is just delightful and the monochrome on colour nesting of the two images works brilliantly.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: A really well seen/constructed image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: DPC is full of cat shots - but this one transcends indulgent pet sentimentality and delivers an unexpected killer punch. The bird on the TV(?) and the transfixed kit is just delightful and the monochrome on colour nesting of the two images works brilliantly. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: A really well seen/constructed image.', '2012-02-04 14:23:07.000000', NULL, 1),
