(6666910, 991343, 57570, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon!', '2012-02-08 01:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666911, 996188, 108580, '<td valign="top">Yes impressive, especially for the sensor size. I out commented myself this challenge. Sorry didn''t get to this. I guess my 7 was comment enough :)</td>', 'Yes impressive, especially for the sensor size. I out commented myself this challenge. Sorry didn''t get to this. I guess my 7 was comment enough :)', '2012-02-08 01:52:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666912, 995135, 141826, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!!!</td>', 'Congratulations!!!', '2012-02-08 01:52:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666913, 996268, 30982, '<td valign="top">You made Paul positively giddy!  I didn''t know that was even possible!  Thank you for that.  And for a very lovely photograph as well.</td>', 'You made Paul positively giddy!  I didn''t know that was even possible!  Thank you for that.  And for a very lovely photograph as well.', '2012-02-08 01:52:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666914, 995852, 57570, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites in this challenge. Congrats on your top 5 finish!</td>', 'This was one of my favorites in this challenge. Congrats on your top 5 finish!', '2012-02-08 01:52:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666915, 991343, 141826, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!!!!</td>', 'Congratulations!!!!', '2012-02-08 01:53:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666916, 996047, 96574, '<td valign="top">congrats on the top 10!<br/>i was hoping this would do well.</td>', 'congrats on the top 10!i was hoping this would do well.', '2012-02-08 01:54:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666918, 993696, 108580, '<td valign="top">Yup there''s the blue hand... :) Oddly I appreciated it enough for a 7. These images are growing on me, like a fungus :)<br/>If you ever win a challenge with a pinhole shot how are you going to validate it? :) Email them a picture of the tin foil with needle hole? hehe.</td>', 'Yup there''s the blue hand... :) Oddly I appreciated it enough for a 7. These images are growing on me, like a fungus :)If you ever win a challenge with a pinhole shot how are you going to validate it? :) Email them a picture of the tin foil with needle hole? hehe.', '2012-02-08 01:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666920, 995600, 108580, '<td valign="top">A Ben dolphin, not bad. 7.</td>', 'A Ben dolphin, not bad. 7.', '2012-02-08 01:58:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666921, 994654, 115307, '<td valign="top">Thanks Harvey, but it was actually my 50mm 1.4. I accidentally set it to the wrong lens. I also did a LOT of blurring and burning of the background in photoshop, so its a lot less impressive then you think. But I am glad you liked the image :-)</td>', 'Thanks Harvey, but it was actually my 50mm 1.4. I accidentally set it to the wrong lens. I also did a LOT of blurring and burning of the background in photoshop, so its a lot less impressive then you think. But I am glad you liked the image :-)', '2012-02-08 01:59:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666922, 995405, 128201, '<td valign="top">This is an absolutely stunning image. IMO it should have placed much higher.</td>', 'This is an absolutely stunning image. IMO it should have placed much higher.', '2012-02-08 02:01:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666927, 996139, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hi Konrad. Take the skew buildings away and this would (again) be right up there. May I suggest trying another but get the building perspective straight and see how it would do? Advanced editing allows it I think. Or shoot more sky and less earth, to get the buildings in the middle of the frame where there''s less distortion. I thought long and hard before getting my Tokina 12-24mm f/4 ATC PRO DX due it''s distortion, but then I seldom photograph buildings with it. I prefer to use the 28mm DG Sigma (=42mm on DX) for that. Saves me PP :)</td>', 'Hi Konrad. Take the skew buildings away and this would (again) be right up there. May I suggest trying another but get the building perspective straight and see how it would do? Advanced editing allows it I think. Or shoot more sky and less earth, to get the buildings in the middle of the frame where there''s less distortion. I thought long and hard before getting my Tokina 12-24mm f/4 ATC PRO DX due it''s distortion, but then I seldom photograph buildings with it. I prefer to use the 28mm DG Sigma (=42mm on DX) for that. Saves me PP :)', '2012-02-08 02:03:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666932, 996126, 96574, '<td valign="top">i love the simplicity in this one. really glad it did well.</td>', 'i love the simplicity in this one. really glad it did well.', '2012-02-08 02:05:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666933, 995228, 108580, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30861" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Bear_Music</a> sells papers?!<br/>ETA: PS: What lens is it then? Nikkor 50mm f/1.4 ? :) You should print a Jumbo and give him copy.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-02-08 02:07:27.</i></td>', ' Bear_Music sells papers?!ETA: PS: What lens is it then? Nikkor 50mm f/1.4 ? :) You should print a Jumbo and give him copy.', '2012-02-08 02:05:52.000000', '2012-02-08 02:07:27.000000', 0),
(6666936, 994676, 30214, '<td valign="top">love the hint of shoes! well done Deb!</td>', 'love the hint of shoes! well done Deb!', '2012-02-08 02:07:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666937, 996441, 96574, '<td valign="top">very nice. i thought for sure this was going to end up in the top 10. still a very strong finish though.</td>', 'very nice. i thought for sure this was going to end up in the top 10. still a very strong finish though.', '2012-02-08 02:07:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666938, 996268, 113156, '<td valign="top">Glorious John, the tones you chose are just splendid, bravo.</td>', 'Glorious John, the tones you chose are just splendid, bravo.', '2012-02-08 02:09:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666939, 996088, 108580, '<td valign="top">Ha! Great take Stephen. Pity about the wind. Love the white takkies. Was she wearing black Nike''s? Crisp and clean and fun.</td>', 'Ha! Great take Stephen. Pity about the wind. Love the white takkies. Was she wearing black Nike''s? Crisp and clean and fun.', '2012-02-08 02:10:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666941, 996346, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hermann. Crisp and sharp, nice colours. Love the muck on everything and the reflection in the sunnies. Face in shade is a bummer though, strips the power out of the shot.</td>', 'Hermann. Crisp and sharp, nice colours. Love the muck on everything and the reflection in the sunnies. Face in shade is a bummer though, strips the power out of the shot.', '2012-02-08 02:19:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666942, 995838, 114233, '<td valign="top">Lovely Harvey! Congrats on the top 10 and narrowly missing the HM. Wonderfully captured - I bet this looks much better at anything larger than 800px!</td>', 'Lovely Harvey! Congrats on the top 10 and narrowly missing the HM. Wonderfully captured - I bet this looks much better at anything larger than 800px!', '2012-02-08 02:21:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666944, 996366, 96574, '<td valign="top">great shot tom!<br/>the focus and composition are perfect.</td>', 'great shot tom!the focus and composition are perfect.', '2012-02-08 02:22:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666945, 996134, 114233, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ammie:</b></div><hr/><i> Ha, a master at work! Great shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>... lots of dedication! Well done Rian. Hope you can get a few more in the next couple of months before the highveld storms leave us again</td>', 'Originally posted by Ammie: Ha, a master at work! Great shot.  ... lots of dedication! Well done Rian. Hope you can get a few more in the next couple of months before the highveld storms leave us again', '2012-02-08 02:23:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666947, 994341, 96574, '<td valign="top">nice, should''ve finished higher i think.<br/>the dof and focus are perfect.<br/> <br/>edit due to my crappy spelling.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-02-08 05:46:02.</i></td>', 'nice, should''ve finished higher i think.the dof and focus are perfect. edit due to my crappy spelling.', '2012-02-08 02:25:49.000000', '2012-02-08 05:46:02.000000', 0),
(6666955, 994487, 108580, '<td valign="top">Amazing how many Views the brown gets :)</td>', 'Amazing how many Views the brown gets :)', '2012-02-08 02:40:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666956, 995405, 117474, '<td valign="top">Would never have guessed this as being yours! Beautiful image. Got an 8 from me. Should have been higher, but didn''t get a chance to go through my votes a second time.</td>', 'Would never have guessed this as being yours! Beautiful image. Got an 8 from me. Should have been higher, but didn''t get a chance to go through my votes a second time.', '2012-02-08 02:41:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666957, 995980, 117474, '<td valign="top">Gah! Beat me by 5 places! Grr! :-)</td>', 'Gah! Beat me by 5 places! Grr! :-)', '2012-02-08 02:42:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666959, 996188, 117474, '<td valign="top">Nice. I really liked this image in voting. Love the blue-to-orange-to-blue from the sky and reflection.</td>', 'Nice. I really liked this image in voting. Love the blue-to-orange-to-blue from the sky and reflection.', '2012-02-08 02:45:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666960, 994492, 117474, '<td valign="top">You definitely achieved emphasis on his height! The phone in his hands is great! I liked this image.</td>', 'You definitely achieved emphasis on his height! The phone in his hands is great! I liked this image.', '2012-02-08 02:47:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666962, 996307, 117474, '<td valign="top">Nice finish!</td>', 'Nice finish!', '2012-02-08 02:50:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666963, 995838, 86218, '<td valign="top">Congrats Harvey!!! Top 10 and like Steve says... just missing HM. Very glad for you. This is your expertise. Lovely shot</td>', 'Congrats Harvey!!! Top 10 and like Steve says... just missing HM. Very glad for you. This is your expertise. Lovely shot', '2012-02-08 02:55:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666964, 991343, 117474, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid I only this a 6. I wish I had the chance to review my votes before rollover, would have bumped it up at least two points. Sorry about that. <br/>But WOW. Incredible image! Congrats on the yellow!</td>', 'I''m afraid I only this a 6. I wish I had the chance to review my votes before rollover, would have bumped it up at least two points. Sorry about that. But WOW. Incredible image! Congrats on the yellow!', '2012-02-08 02:57:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666965, 996389, 57570, '<td valign="top">Absolutely gorgeous. Congrats on top 5!</td>', 'Absolutely gorgeous. Congrats on top 5!', '2012-02-08 02:59:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666966, 995838, 57570, '<td valign="top">Nice poster perfect shot! Congrats.</td>', 'Nice poster perfect shot! Congrats.', '2012-02-08 03:00:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666967, 996092, 137103, '<td valign="top">I meant to comment before it finished, but this was hands down my favorite of the free study.</td>', 'I meant to comment before it finished, but this was hands down my favorite of the free study.', '2012-02-08 03:04:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666968, 994654, 108580, '<td valign="top">You''re welcome. All I had was 50mm f/1.4 too. No such thing as money for UWA 10-20mm''s in my heyday.<br/>All the same it''s great work and I hope the paper published it? If they didn''t submit it to your local rag too!</td>', 'You''re welcome. All I had was 50mm f/1.4 too. No such thing as money for UWA 10-20mm''s in my heyday.All the same it''s great work and I hope the paper published it? If they didn''t submit it to your local rag too!', '2012-02-08 03:04:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6666969, 996475, 117474, '<td valign="top">Nice image! Did you wash him before shooting? He looks really clean! :-) Really suits the background. Great finish! <br/>Thanks for the comments. Never realised animals were repetitive like that. Will keep it in mind in future! <br/> <br/>As far as I know, I think it''s meant to be "Snaffles and me" in the situation of your second sentence. Remove "Snaffles" from the sentence and you''d use "me" and (so I''ve been told multiple times by people who apparently understand grammar) you use "me" rather than "I" in that context. Weird, eh?</td>', 'Nice image! Did you wash him before shooting? He looks really clean! :-) Really suits the background. Great finish! Thanks for the comments. Never realised animals were repetitive like that. Will keep it in mind in future!  As far as I know, I think it''s meant to be "Snaffles and me" in the situation of your second sentence. Remove "Snaffles" from the sentence and you''d use "me" and (so I''ve been told multiple times by people who apparently understand grammar) you use "me" rather than "I" in that context. Weird, eh?', '2012-02-08 03:05:43.000000', NULL, 0),
